    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>On 10 July 1940 the National Assembly of the Third Republic voted by 569 to 80 to grant full powers to Pétain, whose regime called itself the French State.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> took antisemitic measures of its own, such as the Law on the status of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of 3 October 1940, and its police organized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vel-dhiv-roundup">Vel' d'Hiv Roundup</a> of July 1942.</li><li>In November 1942, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> landed in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, German and Italian forces occupied all of Metropolitan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, ending any pretence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a>'s independence.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> replaced Marianne with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> as the national symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and its &quot;francisque&quot; insignia arranged a Gallic baton and double-headed hatchet to resemble the fasces.</p></aside>
    </section>

